**Summary:**

I found and fixed the off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The bug was that the function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which meant it was returning the second word instead of the first word. This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail (returned 'world' instead of 'hello')
- `test_single` to error (tried to access index 1 when only index 0 exists)

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`. All tests now pass successfully.
